rs, mule, sandals, sneakers, sports, thongs, and toe ring shoes, as well as heel footwear. It is also involved in kids' footwear; apparel, including joggers and bottoms, shorts, t-shirt, and Polos for men and women; and accessories, such as belts, handbags, laptop bags, belts, wallets, school bags, and other bags. In addition, the company sells its products primarily under Bata, Hush Puppies, Nine West, North Star, Power, Bata Red Label, Bata Comfit, Bubblegummers, Disney, Naturalizer, Marie Claire, Scholl, Floatz by Bata, Weinbrenner, and Bata Industrials brand names through retail and franchisee stores, a wholesale network, and e-commerce. The company was formerly known as Bata Shoe Company Private Limited and changed its name to Bata India Limited in 1973. Bata India Limited was incorporated in 1931 and is based in Gurugram, India. Bata India Limited operates as a subsidiary of Bata (BN) B.V.","beta":0.352,"sharesOutstanding":128527540,"marketCap":81614987264,"trailingPE":54.2735,"forwardPE":31.2544,"priceToBook":6.5751,"enterpriseToEbitda":20.546,"dividendYield":5.36,"heldPercentInsiders":0.5047,"heldPercentInstitutions":0.3106,"earningsGrowth":0.306,"revenueGrowth":0.075,"website":"https://www.bata.in","fullTimeEmployees":3602,"recommendationKey":"hold","targetMeanPrice":658.3571,"numberOfAnalystOpinions":14,"financialCurrency":"INR"},"estimates":{"eps":{"0q":{"avg":6.02,"low":6.02,"high":6.02,"yearAgoEps":5.5984,"numberOfAnalysts":1.0,"growth":0.0753,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"+1q":{"avg":1.81,"low":1.81,"high":1.81,"yearAgoEps":1.4237,"numberOfAnalysts":1.0,"growth":0.2713,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"0y":{"avg":16.5886,"low":14.22,"high":18.6,"yearAgoEps":13.252,"numberOfAnalysts":8.0,"growth":0.2518,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"+1y":{"avg":20.3171,"low":17.6,"high":23.7,"yearAgoEps":16.5886,"numberOfAnalysts":9.0,"growth":0.2248,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"}},"revenue":{"0q":{"avg":10166245